From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Koval <kovalidis@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:18:34 +0200
Subject: Run optional install hook of the custom rootfs overlay

After copying custom-overlay into the rootfs, run its .install.sh (if
executable) with the target dir, for what plain files can't do, such as
editing generated files like /etc/shadow. The hook itself is not copied.

Also fix the check for the overlay root dir, which tested an empty path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 common/overlays/rootfs/custom/install.sh | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/overlays/rootfs/custom/install.sh b/common/overlays/rootfs/custom/install.sh
index e52c16d..5826e0e 100755
--- a/common/overlays/rootfs/custom/install.sh
+++ b/common/overlays/rootfs/custom/install.sh
@@ -5,8 +5,13 @@ TARGET_DIR="$1"
 
 OVERLAY_DIR="$(dirname "$(realpath "$0")")"
 
-if [ ! -d "" ]; then
+if [ ! -d "$OVERLAY_DIR/root" ]; then
 	mkdir -p $OVERLAY_DIR/root
 fi
 
-$RK_RSYNC "$OVERLAY_DIR/root/" "$TARGET_DIR/"
+$RK_RSYNC --exclude /.install.sh "$OVERLAY_DIR/root/" "$TARGET_DIR/"
+
+# Optional hook for what plain files can't do (edit generated files, ...)
+if [ -x "$OVERLAY_DIR/root/.install.sh" ]; then
+	"$OVERLAY_DIR/root/.install.sh" "$TARGET_DIR"
+fi
